---
title: "12 · FAQ"
description: Answers to common questions about invoices, numbers, GST, payments and corrections.
sidebar:
  order: 13
  label: "12 · FAQ"
---

## Why is Issue greyed out?

The reason is written next to the button. The most common ones: the changes are not saved yet (select **Save changes** first), the invoice has no line, or the total is zero or less. A draft from a floating-quote contract needs its amount set first.

## The editor says the document cannot be issued yet. What do I do?

The note names what is missing, for example the client's address or the issuer's GST registration number, and links to where it is added. Complete the client's record, or ask a tenant admin to complete the issuing entity or its GST registration number, then issue again. The draft has not taken a number. See [Details a tax invoice must show](/en/invoices/issue-send/#details-a-tax-invoice-must-show).

## How do I bill only the first installment of a contract?

Select **Create invoice** on the signed contract. In **Choose installments**, the next installment of each line is ticked; leave it as it is and select **Continue**. Raise the next installment later in the same way. See [Bill a contract by its installments](/en/invoices/create/#bill-a-contract-by-its-installments).

## Can an installment be billed twice?

No. An installment on a draft or an issued invoice cannot be chosen again. Void the invoice or delete the draft to free it; a credit note does not free it.

## Can I type a name that is not in the service catalog?

No. Each line must be a service from the service catalog. Ask the department head to add the service to the catalog (see [Services & Packages](/en/crm/services-packages/)).

## Can I enter the GST amount by hand?

No. GST is calculated from each line's tax code and the issuing entity's GST registration, and cannot be added as an adjustment.

## Why is the title "Tax Invoice" and not the title in the template?

A GST-registered issuing entity always issues a tax invoice, so Operon prints **Tax Invoice** as the title.

## The invoice has a mistake but it is already issued. What do I do?

- No payment or credit recorded yet: open the invoice, select **Edit invoice**, correct it and select **Save changes**. It keeps its number, and its PDF is produced again.
- A payment or credit is recorded: ask a manager to create a credit note for the difference (see [Credit notes](/en/invoices/credit-notes/)).
- The issuing entity is wrong: ask a manager to void the invoice, then duplicate it, correct the duplicate and issue it.

## The client paid more than the invoice. What do I do?

Record the full amount received. The invoice becomes **Paid**, and the rest is kept as an overpayment for the client. A manager can later apply it to another invoice of the same client, issuing entity and currency, or record a refund. See [Overpayments](/en/invoices/overpayments/).

## The overpayment was recorded in error. How do I undo it?

Ask a manager to delete the payment on the overpaid invoice. The overpayment is voided with it. If part of the overpayment has already been applied or refunded, remove those first.

## Does an overpayment have GST or a PDF?

No. An overpayment is not a supply. It has no GST, no number and no PDF, and it is not sent to the client.

## The client's price includes GST. How do I enter it?

Set **Amounts are** to **Tax inclusive** on the editor's **Settings** tab, and enter the price including GST. Operon works the GST back from it. See [Tax-inclusive amounts](/en/invoices/edit/#tax-inclusive-amounts).

## Where do I put the client's purchase order number?

In **Reference** on the editor's **Association** tab. It is printed on the invoice and can be searched in the invoice list.

## Can I delete an issued invoice?

No. An issued invoice can only be voided, by a manager, with a reason. It keeps its number.

## Why can I not void this invoice?

A payment or applied credit is recorded on it. Delete the payments and remove the applied credit first. Only managers and tenant admins can void.

## The client paid by bank transfer. Will the invoice update by itself?

No, unless the issuing entity is linked to Xero. Payments are not collected or matched automatically: record the payment on the invoice (see [Record payments](/en/invoices/payments/)). When the issuing entity is linked to Xero, the payment is recorded in Xero and appears on the invoice after the next sync.

## Why is there no Record payment button?

The invoice's issuing entity is linked to Xero, so its payments are recorded in Xero, or the invoice was imported from Xero. Record or change the payment in Xero.

## Can I connect Xero?

A tenant admin connects Xero from **Invoice settings** › **Third-party connections**. See [Connect Xero](/en/invoices/settings-reminders/#connect-xero).

## Does the client receive the PDF as an attachment?

No. The email carries a link. The client opens the online copy and downloads the PDF from there.

## The client says the link does not work.

The invoice may have been voided; a void invoice's link no longer opens. Otherwise, copy the link again from **More** › **Copy online link** and send it to the client.

## Why did the client not receive a payment reminder?

Check, in order: automatic reminders are on for the organisation (**Automatically email payment reminders to clients** in **Invoice settings**; they are off for a new organisation); the invoice has been emailed at least once; **Payment reminders for this client** is on in the client's **Invoices** tab; **Payment reminders on** is switched on in the invoice's **Delivery** card; the invoice still has an amount due; and a reminder rule is switched on for that day in **Invoice settings**. Only a tenant admin can open **Invoice settings**; ask one to check the rules.

## Does a change to a template change old invoices?

No. Each invoice keeps the layout it was created with.

## Can I invoice in a currency other than SGD?

Not in this release. Invoices are raised in SGD.
